unit psx;
{ psx - the Kobold binding to the libpsx PlayStation SDK (milestone 6).

  An umbrella over the per-subsystem leaves under psx/ (psx.gpu, psx.pad,
  psx.spu, psx.fixed, psx.tex, psx.cd, psx.gte, psx.ot). A game does `uses psx`
  and reaches every call, GpuInit, DrawRect, PadRead, Beep, the GTE helpers, and
  the fixed-point math, through this one re-export.

  The split keeps the binary small. Each leaf lowers to its own object, so the
  linker pulls only the leaves a program references, and each leaf draws in only
  its own libpsx members. A 2D game no longer carries the GTE, ordering-table,
  texture, sound, and CD code it never calls. The leaves are a thin pass-through:
  they declare the libpsx C entry points as external cdecl and expose them under
  Kobold names, adding no logic of their own. Kobold and libpsx share the toolkit
  stack calling convention. }
uses
  psx.gpu, psx.pad, psx.spu, psx.fixed, psx.tex, psx.cd, psx.gte, psx.ot;

interface

reexport psx.gpu, psx.pad, psx.spu, psx.fixed, psx.tex, psx.cd, psx.gte, psx.ot;

implementation

end.
